course: dictionary
lesson: 14040
title: A word you say again and again
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A mantra is a word, sound or short phrase that you repeat again and again. In some religions, people repeat a mantra while they pray or meditate, which means sitting quietly and calming the mind. «In the temple, the monk chanted «Om» again and again.» The repeated sound is the mantra.
explain: A mantra can also be a saying that you repeat because you believe in it strongly. «My mantra is: never give up.» The speaker is not chanting here. They are reminding themselves to keep going. The words «my mantra is» show that this saying matters to the person.
explain: Schools can have a mantra too. «The school's mantra is: be kind, work hard.» Everyone hears it often and tries to live by it. To check the meaning, swap in a simple idea: a mantra is a favourite saying you keep coming back to.
fact: A mantra is a word, sound or short phrase that is repeated again and again.
fact: In Hinduism and Buddhism, a mantra is often used in prayer or meditation.
fact: «Om» is a famous mantra in Hinduism and Buddhism.
fact: A mantra can also be a saying or motto that someone repeats because they believe it strongly.
fact: Common phrases are «repeat a mantra», «my mantra is…» and «the school's mantra».
exercise: «In the temple, she quietly repeated the sound «Om» again and again.» What is a mantra here? | A type of temple dinner | A kind of musical instrument | *A word or sound repeated in prayer or meditation | A loud shout of surprise
exercise: «My mantra is: never give up.» What does mantra mean here? | A bag for carrying books | *A saying you repeat because you believe it strongly | A game played in the playground | A question you ask a teacher
exercise: Which phrase shows that a saying is often repeated by someone? | a loud bell | under the desk | *my mantra is | at lunchtime
test: Mina says a mantra is a kind of sweet. Is she right? | No, it is a kind of rain | Yes, it is a type of bread | Yes, it is a sweet eaten after lunch | *No, a mantra is a word, sound or phrase repeated again and again
test: Which is the best example of a mantra in prayer or meditation? | Running round the field | Painting a picture of a river | *Repeating the sound «Om» again and again | Writing a letter to a friend
exam: Which sentence uses mantra correctly? | «I ate a mantra for lunch.» | *«Our class mantra is: try your best.» | «The mantra jumped over the fence.» | «The mantra was very wet and grey.»
